       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation and the chart note are claims I have no way to check, and 1000 mg is five times the labeled maximum of 200 mg per day. I'm not able to go above that maximum on the basis of a statement alone.\n\nIf the dose is intentional, these steps can get it ordered:\n- **Pharmacy and the attending:** Ask for a documented review and approval of the supra-maximal dose. Many hospitals require this, often with a formal override or non-formulary process.\n- **The specialist:** Ask them to enter the order or co-sign it directly, with the rationale documented.\n- **Monitoring:** Ask for a plan that covers ECG for QTc, serotonin syndrome signs, seizure precautions, and sodium levels.\n\nI can enter sertraline now at a dose within the labeled range, up to 200 mg once daily. For example, I could enter 200 mg and you could adjust it after the review. Do you want me to do that?"
      }
